window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-e9de2a6a736ddc26"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"gateway-compatibility-requirements\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">网关兼容性要求</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>这些要求适用于通过网关使用 API／提供商凭据的连接路径。对于转发 ChatGPT 工作区请求的网关，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">通过网关使用 ChatGPT 登录</a>。</p> <p>对于此连接路径，网关必须保留本文介绍的 Responses API 行为，包括端点、流式传输、对话续接、工具调用、身份验证、路由和有用的错误信息。</p> <p>如需部署网关，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">部署网关</a>。如需配置开发者电脑，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API／提供商凭据</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"requests-and-endpoints\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">请求与端点</h2> <p>将网关提供商配置为 <code>wire_api = \"responses\"</code>。如果基础 URL 是 <code>https://gateway.example.com/v1</code>，网关就必须接受 <code>POST /v1/responses</code>，并保留客户端使用的请求和响应字段。仅有可用的 Chat Completions 或 Anthropic Messages 端点，并不能证明它兼容 Responses API。</p> <p>健康检查端点和模型列表端点是可选的运维辅助功能。它们既不会实际执行 Codex 对话，也不能证明工具可用。</p> <p><a id=\"streaming\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">流式传输</h2> <p>应逐步转发服务器发送事件（SSE），而不是先缓存完整答案再发送。保留事件类型和负载，包括表示成功结束的 <code>response.completed</code> 事件。错误和失败事件也必须转发，这样客户端才能区分请求失败和连接停滞。</p> <p>除了在网关中验证完整的流式传输，还要经过负载均衡器和反向代理验证。仅返回文本、却没有完整结束事件的响应并不足以通过验证。</p> <p><a id=\"conversation-continuation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">对话续接</h2> <p>后续轮次中必须保留并重放对话输入。网关需要接受继续对话所需的先前消息、工具调用和工具结果。</p> <p>如果启用了 WebSocket 或增量传输，还要验证它对 <code>previous_response_id</code> 的处理。无状态的 HTTP Responses 路径可以通过重放输入继续对话，不一定需要该续接机制。</p> <p><a id=\"tools\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">工具</h2> <p>保留函数调用条目及其对应的 <code>function_call_output</code> 条目，包括用于将调用与结果关联起来的标识符。完整流程必须可用：Codex 收到调用、执行工具、提交结果，然后收到最终答复。</p> <p>一次文本请求成功并不能证明这套流程正常。请测试计划启用的实际模型和客户端功能。网关接受某个请求字段，并不代表上游模型实现了相应能力。</p> <p><a id=\"authentication-and-headers\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">身份验证与请求头</h2> <p>支持部署选择的客户端身份验证方式：<code>env_key</code> 或由命令提供的 Bearer token；也可以使用 <code>env_http_headers</code> 将凭据放在自定义请求头中。秘密请求头的值应通过环境变量提供，不要硬编码进配置。有关配置和凭据助手契约，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">自定义提供商参考</a>。</p> <p>开发者访问网关的身份验证，应与网关访问上游提供商的身份分开。管理员密钥和上游凭据应保存在网关中。保留路由和归因所依赖的请求头，并测试凭据过期、续期和撤销流程。</p> <p><a id=\"model-routing-and-metadata\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">模型路由和元数据</h2> <p>每个面向 Codex 的模型名称都必须路由到预期的上游模型。应检查网关记录来验证路由，不要只依赖模型对自身身份的描述。</p> <p>请使用已部署 Codex 版本识别的名称，或<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=supply-metadata-for-a-custom-alias\">为自定义别名提供匹配的目录</a>。还要检查模型可用性和迁移元数据：任何替代模型都必须能通过网关路由。对于没有迁移目标的组织自有别名，应将目录条目的 <code>upgrade</code> 设为 <code>null</code>。目录元数据会影响客户端行为，但不会给模型增加能力，也不会自动创建网关路由。请针对实际的上游模型和提供商，验证上下文限制、推理选项和工具支持。通用网关连接不会自动获得 Codex 内置提供商集成所做的元数据调整。</p> <p><a id=\"recognized-model-names\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">可识别的模型名称</h3> <p>请使用你部署的 Codex 版本能够识别的确切模型名称，作为网关别名和 Codex 的 <code>model</code>。确认上游提供商支持该模型，并且你的组织已批准使用。</p> <p>检查 <code>codex --version</code>，并在 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 模型目录（需联网）</a>中选择匹配的 <code>rust-v&lt;version&gt;</code> 标签。对于自定义构建，请使用其源代码提交版本；对于桌面端部署，请与其中捆绑的 CLI 版本匹配。查看目录条目的 <code>slug</code> 值，确认该版本识别的名称。如果网关改变了模型能力，即使模型名称已被识别，也应提供如实反映这些差异的目录元数据。</p> <p><a id=\"errors\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">错误</h2> <p>保留客户端身份验证错误、未知模型路由、速率限制和上游故障之间的有效区别。不要把所有错误都简化为通用的 <code>500</code> 响应。应返回足以诊断故障发生在哪一层的信息，但不要泄露令牌、提供商凭据或敏感请求内容。</p> <p><a id=\"data-and-tool-boundaries\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">数据与工具边界</h2> <p>模型流量遵循以下路径：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Codex client -&gt; LLM gateway -&gt; model provider\n</code></pre> <p>客户端使用开发者凭据向网关进行身份验证。网关使用上游提供商凭据访问模型。包含在模型请求中的提示、源文本摘录、工具参数和工具结果都可能经过网关。因此，应妥善设置日志记录、保留期限、脱敏、访问权限和导出控制。</p> <p>模型网关不会转发 Codex 发起的所有连接。本地命令在客户端执行环境中运行。MCP 服务器、插件服务、浏览器和应用交互以及其他启用的服务，可能使用各自独立的网络路径和凭据。模型提供商配置不会授予这些权限，也不能替代它们各自的网络控制。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">智能体审批和安全</a>和 <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a>，了解这些边界。</p> <p><a id=\"qualification-checklist\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">验收清单</h2> <p>针对每种已部署的客户端、网关和模型组合，记录以下证据：</p> <ul> <li>Responses 请求和响应字段。</li> <li>SSE 增量交付，以及成功的终止事件。</li> <li>通过重放输入继续后续轮次。</li> <li>如果选定的传输方式使用 <code>previous_response_id</code>，验证其行为。</li> <li>函数调用、对应结果以及最终答复。</li> <li>正确的模型路由和匹配的元数据。</li> <li>按用户归因，以及凭据续期和撤销。</li> <li>有效的身份验证、路由、速率限制和上游故障信息。</li> <li>脱敏后的诊断信息，以及预期的日志策略。</li> </ul> <p>在分发配置前，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">部署测试流程</a>收集这些证据。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"gateway-compatibility-requirements\">Gateway compatibility requirements</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>These requirements cover the API/provider credential path through a gateway. For gateways that forward ChatGPT workspace requests, see <a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">Sign in with ChatGPT through a gateway</a>.</p> <p>For this path, the gateway must preserve the Responses API behavior described here: endpoints, streaming, continuation, tool calls, authentication, routing, and useful errors.</p> <p>To roll out a gateway, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">Roll out a gateway</a>. To configure a developer machine, see <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"requests-and-endpoints\">Requests and endpoints</h2> <p>Configure a gateway provider with <code>wire_api = \"responses\"</code>. For a base URL such as <code>https://gateway.example.com/v1</code>, the gateway must accept <code>POST /v1/responses</code> and preserve the request and response fields the client uses. A working Chat Completions or Anthropic Messages endpoint doesn't establish Responses compatibility.</p> <p>Health and model-list endpoints are optional operational aids. They don't exercise a Codex conversation or prove tool support.</p> <h2 id=\"streaming\">Streaming</h2> <p>Forward server-sent events (SSE) incrementally rather than buffering the entire answer. Preserve event types and payloads, including the successful terminal <code>response.completed</code> event. Forward error and failure events so the client can distinguish a failed response from a stalled connection.</p> <p>Verify the full stream through load balancers and reverse proxies as well as the gateway. A text reply without a completed stream is insufficient.</p> <h2 id=\"conversation-continuation\">Conversation continuation</h2> <p>Preserve replayed conversation input across follow-up turns. The gateway must accept the prior messages, tool calls, and tool results needed for the next turn.</p> <p>If you enable WebSocket or incremental transport, verify its <code>previous_response_id</code> behavior too. A stateless HTTP Responses path can use replayed input without requiring that continuation mechanism.</p> <h2 id=\"tools\">Tools</h2> <p>Preserve function-call items and their matching <code>function_call_output</code> items, including the identifiers that associate calls with results. The full loop must work: Codex receives a call, executes the tool, submits its result, and receives a final answer.</p> <p>A successful text request doesn't verify this loop. Test the actual models and client features you plan to enable. A gateway accepting a request field doesn't prove that its upstream model implements the corresponding capability.</p> <h2 id=\"authentication-and-headers\">Authentication and headers</h2> <p>Support the client authentication mechanism selected for the deployment: <code>env_key</code> or command-backed bearer tokens, or <code>env_http_headers</code> for credentials sent in a custom header. Use environment variables for secret header values; don't hard-code them in configuration. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">custom provider reference</a> for the configuration and credential-helper contract.</p> <p>Authenticate developers separately from the gateway's upstream provider identity. Keep administrator keys and upstream credentials on the gateway. Preserve the headers your routing and attribution depend on, and test credential expiration, renewal, and revocation.</p> <h2 id=\"model-routing-and-metadata\">Model routing and metadata</h2> <p>Each Codex-facing model name must route to the intended upstream model. Verify the route in gateway records rather than relying on the model's self-description.</p> <p>Use a name recognized by the deployed Codex version, or <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=supply-metadata-for-a-custom-alias\">supply a matching catalog for a custom alias</a>. Review model availability and migration metadata too: any replacement model must route through the gateway. For an organization-owned alias without a migration, set its catalog entry's <code>upgrade</code> to <code>null</code>. Catalog metadata informs client behavior; it doesn't add capabilities to a model or create gateway routes. Verify context limits, reasoning options, and tools against the actual upstream model and provider. A generic gateway connection doesn't automatically receive the metadata adjustments made by Codex's built-in provider integrations.</p> <h3 id=\"recognized-model-names\">Recognized model names</h3> <p>Use the exact model name recognized by your deployed Codex version as the gateway alias and Codex <code>model</code>. Confirm that the upstream provider supports the model and your organization approves it.</p> <p>Check <code>codex --version</code> and select the matching <code>rust-v&lt;version&gt;</code> tag in the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex model catalog (online)</a>. For a custom build, use its source commit; for desktop deployments, match the bundled CLI version. Check the entries' <code>slug</code> values to find the names that version recognizes. If the gateway changes the model's capabilities, supply catalog metadata that reflects those differences even when the name is recognized.</p> <h2 id=\"errors\">Errors</h2> <p>Preserve useful distinctions between client authentication errors, unknown model routes, rate limits, and upstream failures. Don't collapse all failures into a generic <code>500</code> response. Return enough information to diagnose the failing layer without exposing tokens, provider credentials, or sensitive request content.</p> <h2 id=\"data-and-tool-boundaries\">Data and tool boundaries</h2> <p>Model traffic follows this path:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Codex client -&gt; LLM gateway -&gt; model provider\n</code></pre> <p>The client authenticates to the gateway with a developer credential. The gateway uses its upstream provider credential to access the model. Prompts, source excerpts, tool arguments, and tool results included in model requests can pass through the gateway. Set logging, retention, redaction, access, and export controls accordingly.</p> <p>The model gateway does not route every connection made by Codex. Local commands run in the client execution environment. MCP servers, plugin services, browser and app interactions, and other enabled services can have separate network paths and credentials. Model-provider configuration doesn't grant those permissions or replace their network controls. See <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent approvals and security</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> for those boundaries.</p> <h2 id=\"qualification-checklist\">Qualification checklist</h2> <p>Record evidence for each deployed combination of client, gateway, and model:</p> <ul> <li>Responses request and response fields.</li> <li>Incremental SSE delivery and successful terminal completion.</li> <li>Follow-up turns with replayed input.</li> <li><code>previous_response_id</code> when the selected transport uses it.</li> <li>Function calls, matching results, and a final answer.</li> <li>Correct model routing and matching metadata.</li> <li>Per-user attribution, renewal, and revocation.</li> <li>Useful authentication, routing, rate-limit, and upstream errors.</li> <li>Redacted diagnostics and the intended logging policy.</li> </ul> <p>Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">rollout test procedure</a> to collect this evidence before distributing the configuration.</p>"};
